ll,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123003","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123003.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123003.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"`PackedSceneEditorTranslationParserPlugin::parse_file` now uses metadata/_tab_name instead of node name when available if a node is a child of a `TabContainer`\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #123002\r\n(tested on the provided MRP)\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI'm pretty sure this change doesn't need to be more complicated, it keeps the previous behavior as a fallback. If the tab title wasn't modified in the inspector, the node's `metadata/_tab_name` will be the same as the node's `name` anyway.\r\n\r\nI noticed that the `metadata/_tab_name` was always at the end of the property list, but reverse iteration seems like premature optimisation.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123003/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}